From: pixel2 ubuntu port
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: refuse CREATE_BUFS on a streaming static-mode capture queue

On HFI 3xx (msm8998) the encoder's bitstream (capture) buffers are in
static mode: the driver registers every capture buffer with
SET_BUFFERS when streaming starts, and the firmware only accepts FTBs
for those addresses. vb2 still lets userspace add buffers with
VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS while the queue streams, and venus queues them like
any other. The firmware then dies on the first FTB of the new buffer:

  qcom-venus: SFR message from FW: QC_IMAGE_VERSION_STRING=VIDEO.VE.4.4-00051
  Err_Fatal - Z:\b\venus_proc\venus\utils\src\vbuffer.c:1219:

and on msm8998 a firmware that has died cannot be restarted (system
error recovery fails 5x, then the SoC resets on the watchdog).

GStreamer's v4l2h264enc/v4l2h265enc do exactly this: when fewer capture
buffers are queued than the pool's copy threshold, the pool
"resurrects" one, i.e. CREATE_BUFS mid-stream (seen as "queued buffer 4"
of 4 allocated; pixel2 test 63). A sink that reads the data (filesink)
hits it every time, fakesink never does; v4l2-ctl never allocates after
STREAMON and works.

Refuse CREATE_BUFS on the capture queue while it streams in static
mode. GStreamer then falls back to copying the buffer, which it already
does when it cannot allocate.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.h
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@
 				u32 buftype);
 int venus_helper_set_color_format(struct venus_inst *inst, u32 fmt);
 int venus_helper_set_dyn_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst);
+bool venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst);
 int venus_helper_set_bufsize(struct venus_inst *inst, u32 bufsize, u32 buftype);
 int venus_helper_set_multistream(struct venus_inst *inst, bool out_en,
 				 bool out2_en);
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
@@ -552,7 +552,13 @@
 		return false;
 
 	return caps->cap_bufs_mode_dynamic;
+}
+
+bool venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst)
+{
+	return is_dynamic_bufmode(inst);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode);
 
 int venus_helper_unregister_bufs(struct venus_inst *inst)
 {
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -1104,6 +1104,17 @@
 		    sizes[0] < inst->output_buf_size)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
+		/*
+		 * In static buffer mode the firmware only knows the bitstream
+		 * buffers registered at stream start; an FTB for a buffer
+		 * created later is a fatal firmware error (msm8998:
+		 * "Err_Fatal - vbuffer.c:1219"). Refuse CREATE_BUFS then.
+		 */
+		if (q->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE &&
+		    vb2_is_streaming(q) &&
+		    !venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(inst))
+			return -EBUSY;
+
 		return 0;
 	}
 
